# Local env files (Mode B uses cross-env inline, so none are needed — this is a safety net so a
# stray local override with a real API base or secret can never be committed).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .env.production is the ONE intentional exception: it holds VITE_POTD_API (the public Worker URL,
# baked into the client bundle anyway — not a secret), so the production Pages build posts to the
# live ratings backend. Committed on purpose.
!.env.production
